      "text": "Illegal entry. Asylum fraud. Gang ties.\n \nA Honduran national and known gang member—tied to the murder of a U.S. citizen in Honduras—tried to game the system, filing a fraudulent asylum claim and living in the U.S. while he waited.\n \nEl Centro Sector agents, working with federal partners, arrested him at a USCIS facility in Tustin during his scheduled asylum appointment. His claim? Revoked.\n \nLet’s be clear: asylum isn’t a loophole for criminals—especially those tied to violent crimes against U.S. citizens.\n \nIf you enter illegally, lie to stay, and bring violence with you—there are consequences.\n \nHe’s now in custody and facing what comes next.\n \n#HonorFirst #PremierSector #USBP #ElCentroSector #DHS #CBP",
